   191|<p>The team gathered around the monitor, watching the data stream across the screen. Each number, each graph, each reading told a story — a story that was only beginning to unfold. They had spent years preparing for this moment, years of training and sacrifice and hope. And now, finally, the moment had arrived.</p>
   192|<p>The room was silent except for the hum of the equipment. No one spoke because no one needed to. They all understood what they were seeing, what it meant, what it would cost. The numbers didn't lie. The truth was there, written in the cold mathematics of the simulation.</p>
   193|<p>"How long?" someone finally asked.</p>
   194|<p>The answer came without hesitation. "We have seventy-two hours. Maybe less."</p>
